<template name="config-menu__enhancements">
    <head>
    </head>
    <body>
        <form class="config__form">
            <div class="config__wrapper">
                <div class="config-debug">
                    <div class="config-debug__scroll">
                        <div class="config-debug-option" data-if="ap_locked == 1">
                            <label class="config-debug-option__label">
                                <div style="flex: 1 1 0dp; width: 100%; white-space: normal;">Connected to Archipelago: the enhancement settings come from your YAML. Connect before starting the game so it boots with them.</div>
                            </label>
                        </div>
                        <div data-if="ap_locked == 0">
                        <div class="config-debug-option" data-if="enh_changed">
                            <label class="config-debug-option__label">
                                <div style="flex: 1 1 0dp; width: 100%; white-space: normal;">Changed settings apply when the game is next launched.</div>
                            </label>
                        </div>
                        <div class="config-debug-option">
                            <label class="config-debug-option__label">
                                <div>Quality of Life</div>
                            </label>
                            <div class="config-debug__option-split">
                                <div class="config-debug__option-controls">
                                    <div class="config-debug__select-wrapper">
                                        <div class="config-debug__select-label" data-event-mouseover="show_tip" data-event-mouseout="hide_tip"><div>JP Healing Amounts</div><div class="config-tip-text">Healing Lv2 restores 16 HP instead of 8, an exact match for the Japanese release (Eltale Monsters).</div></div>
                                        <select data-value="enh_jp_healing" id="enh_jp_healing_select" style="nav-up: #tab_enhancements">
                                            <option value="0">Off</option>
                                            <option value="1">On</option>
                                        </select>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="config-debug__select-wrapper">
                                        <div class="config-debug__select-label" data-event-mouseover="show_tip" data-event-mouseout="hide_tip"><div>JP Magic barrier (+2 Turns)</div><div class="config-tip-text">Magic Barrier holds two turns longer per cast, as in the Japanese release: the roll of attacks it absorbs is raised by two and kept between 3 and 6.</div></div>
                                        <select data-value="enh_longer_magic_barrier" id="enh_longer_magic_barrier_select">
                                            <option value="0">Off</option>
                                            <option value="1">On</option>
                                        </select>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="config-debug__select-wrapper">
                                        <div class="config-debug__select-label" data-event-mouseover="show_tip" data-event-mouseout="hide_tip"><div>JP Stat Up Effect</div><div class="config-tip-text">A burst of colour over Brian whenever one of his stats goes up, as in the Japanese release: red for HP, blue for MP, yellow for defense, green for agility. The US game has no effect at all; this one is drawn over the picture, so it follows Brian on screen.</div></div>
                                        <select data-value="enh_stat_up_effect" id="enh_stat_up_effect_select">
                                            <option value="0">Off</option>
                                            <option value="1">On</option>
                                        </select>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="config-debug__select-wrapper">
                                        <div class="config-debug__select-label" data-event-mouseover="show_tip" data-event-mouseout="hide_tip"><div>Exit from anywhere</div><div class="config-tip-text">The control you bind to "Exit Spell" under Controls warps you to the start of the area without owning the spell or paying its MP. It does nothing during a battle, a menu or a transition, and with this off the binding does nothing at all.</div></div>
                                        <select data-value="enh_exit_from_anywhere" id="enh_exit_from_anywhere_select">
                                            <option value="0">Off</option>
                                            <option value="1">On</option>
                                        </select>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="config-debug__select-wrapper">
                                        <div class="config-debug__select-label" data-event-mouseover="show_tip" data-event-mouseout="hide_tip"><div>Faster walking</div><div class="config-tip-text">Brian moves 50% faster. The game's own collision still runs on every step, and the slide after you let go of the stick lasts the same number of frames as normal. Does nothing on top of Hard Mode, which sets its own pace.</div></div>
                                        <select data-value="enh_faster_walk" id="enh_faster_walk_select">
                                            <option value="0">Off</option>
                                            <option value="1">On</option>
                                        </select>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="config-debug-option">
                            <label class="config-debug-option__label">
                                <div>Fun</div>
                            </label>
                            <div class="config-debug__option-split">
                                <div class="config-debug__option-controls">
                                    <div class="config-debug__select-wrapper">
                                        <div class="config-debug__select-label" data-event-mouseover="show_tip" data-event-mouseout="hide_tip"><div>One Hit KO</div><div class="config-tip-text">Every monster and boss has 1 HP, and so does Brian: his max HP is held at 1, so the first hit ends it for either side. Also applies to a save already in progress.</div></div>
                                        <select data-value="enh_one_hit_ko" id="enh_one_hit_ko_select">
                                            <option value="0">Off</option>
                                            <option value="1">On</option>
                                        </select>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="config-debug__select-wrapper">
                                        <div class="config-debug__select-label" data-event-mouseover="show_tip" data-event-mouseout="hide_tip"><div>N64 Mode</div><div class="config-tip-text">Renders the way the console did: original resolution and aspect ratio, no anti-aliasing and the original HUD layout. Applies straight away, and switching it off puts your previous graphics settings back.</div></div>
                                        <select data-value="enh_n64_mode" id="enh_n64_mode_select">
                                            <option value="0">Off</option>
                                            <option value="1">On</option>
                                        </select>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="config-tip"></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </form>
    </body>
</template>
